  "id": "benton-visual-retention-test",
  "term": "Benton Visual Retention Test",
  "definition": "The Benton Visual Retention Test (BVRT) is a drawing-based task in which a person reproduces visual designs, and performance can be judged by the accuracy of those reproductions. In the source material, it is used to study shape recognition and the reconstruction of visual forms, including simple, medium, and complex designs.",
